body:
Addendum:

While in the background, the application is mostly paused, in a deep sleep. With rendering being paused entirely. I do this by assigning a signal to FocusExited and FocusEntered of the main window of course.

Code that executes on that signal follows:
```
            bool paused = !Busy && !MainWindow.HasFocus();
            OS.LowProcessorUsageMode = paused;
            OS.LowProcessorUsageModeSleepUsec = 100000;
            MainWindow.GetTree().Paused = paused;
            RenderingServer.RenderLoopEnabled = !paused;
```

This will run fine for hours on end and even happily responds accurately to rapidly tabbing in and out of the application for minutes on end. The crash really just happens randomly when it has been sitting idly in the background for hours. No rendering, CPU in low mode, script execution on pause.
